#: ../../source/jupyter-live-kernel_SKILL.md:140
msgid "Practical Tips from Experience"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jupyter-live-kernel_SKILL.md:142
msgid ""
"**First execution after server start may timeout** — the kernel needs a "
"moment to initialize. If you get a timeout, just retry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jupyter-live-kernel_SKILL.md:145
msgid ""
"**The kernel Python is JupyterLab's Python** — packages must be installed"
" in that environment. If you need additional packages, install them into "
"the JupyterLab tool environment first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jupyter-live-kernel_SKILL.md:149
msgid ""
"**--compact flag saves significant tokens** — always use it. JSON output "
"can be very verbose without it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jupyter-live-kernel_SKILL.md:152
msgid ""
"**For pure REPL use**, create a scratch.ipynb and don't bother with cell "
"editing. Just use `execute` repeatedly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jupyter-live-kernel_SKILL.md:155
msgid ""
"**Argument order matters** — subcommand flags like `--path` go BEFORE the"
" sub-subcommand. E.g.: `variables --path nb.ipynb list` not `variables "
"list --path nb.ipynb`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jupyter-live-kernel_SKILL.md:158
msgid ""
"**If a session doesn't exist yet**, you need to start one via the REST "
"API (see Setup section). The tool can't execute without a live kernel "
"session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jupyter-live-kernel_SKILL.md:161
msgid ""
"**Errors are returned as JSON** with traceback — read the `ename` and "
"`evalue` fields to understand what went wrong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jupyter-live-kernel_SKILL.md:164
msgid ""
"**Occasional websocket timeouts** — some operations may timeout on first "
"try, especially after a kernel restart. Retry once before escalating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jupyter-live-kernel_SKILL.md:167
msgid "Timeout Defaults"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/jupyter-live-kernel_SKILL.md:169
msgid ""
"The script has a 30-second default timeout per execution. For long-"
"running operations, pass `--timeout 120`. Use generous timeouts (60+) for"
" initial setup or heavy computation."
msgstr ""

